  "summary": "The study fabricated eight Ti3C2Tx film electrodes: four unfilled MXene films (Ori-M and three proton-acid-treated films) and four corresponding SWCNT-containing composites. MXene was obtained by LiF/HCl in situ HF etching, followed by proton-acid colloidal treatment to pH 3, 1, or 0.5 where applicable; films were vacuum-filtered. The primary electrode, pH1MC, was a stated 95% Ti3C2Tx/5% SWCNT composite and delivered 270.5 F/g at 5 mV/s in 1 m H2SO4. The paper does not report mass loading, thickness, BET surface area, pore characteristics, or numeric capacitances for the pH3M, pH0.5M, pH3MC, and pH0.5MC films."
